This namelist performs a pancake collapse simulation with dark matter and gas.
You need a ascii file for the initial conditions. You can execute the script
python3 ./utils/py/pancake.py
This will generate a file named ic_part in the parent folder.
The script options --delta_ini and --aexp_ini (defaults 0.1 and 0.01) must match
delta_ini and aexp_ini in the INIT_PARAMS block below.
To compile the code with MPI (recommended), type in folder /bin the command line:
make NDIM=1 MPI=1 UNITS=COSMO GRAV=1 HYDRO=1 NPSCAL=1 INIT=PANCAKE
Then execute the code in the parent folder using:
mpirun -np 2 bin/ramses1d namelist/pancake_gas.nml

&RUN_PARAMS
cosmo=.true.
pic=.true.
poisson=.true.
hydro=.true.
nrestart=0
nsubcycle=1,1,2
ncontrol=1
verbose=.false.
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
delta_aout=0.1
aend=1.0
/

&INIT_PARAMS
filetype='ascii'
initfile(1)='.'
H0=72.
omega_m=0.3
omega_l=0.7
boxlen_ini=25.
aexp_ini=0.01
delta_ini=0.1
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=10
levelmax=10
ngridmax=20000
npartmax=40000
nexpand=1,
/

&POISSON_PARAMS
epsilon=1.d-6
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.6666667
courant_factor=0.5
slope_type=2
dual_energy=0.01
entropy=.true.
riemann='hllc'
/

&REFINE_PARAMS
m_refine=10*8.,
/
